  <ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInAndImportantAdditionsToFranchiseRightsTextBlock id="f-1" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Item 1 - N/A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfChangesInAndImportantAdditionsToFranchiseRightsTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfAcquisitionOfOwnershipInOtherCompaniesByReorganizationMergerOrConsolidationWithOtherCompaniesTextBlock id="f-2" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div style="margin-top:2pt;padding-right:18pt"&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%"&gt;Item 2 - N/A&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfAcquisitionOfOwnershipInOtherCompaniesByReorganizationMergerOrConsolidationWithOtherCompaniesTextBlock>
  <ferc:DisclosureOfPurchaseOrSaleOfAnOperatingUnitOrSystemTextBlock id="f-3" contextRef="c-1">&lt;div&gt;&lt;span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:112%"&gt;Item 3 - On May 1, 2026, Northwest Pipeline LLC acquired the Kelso-Beaver (KB) Pipeline from Portland General Electric Company, KB Pipeline Company, and B-R Pipeline, LLC pursuant to the authorization granted in FERC Docket No. CP25-89-000. The acquired facilities are located in Cowlitz County, Washington and consist of the existing Kelso-Beaver Pipeline system. The total purchase price for the acquisition was $2,441,146.97.&lt;/span&gt;&lt;/div&gt;</ferc:DisclosureOfPurchaseOrSaleOfAnOperatingUnitOrSystemTextBlock>
