    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-9" id="fn-9" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#111111;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Gas Received as Imbalances reflects the gas recorded (Northwest&#8217;s imbalances are cleared through in-kind exchanges and reflects the net change) in account 806 that relates to OBA, Receiving Party, Shipper and Park and Loan imbalances.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-10" id="fn-10" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#111111;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Other Gas Withdrawn from Storage relates to system balancing.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-11" id="fn-11" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:3pt;text-align:justify">
        <span style="color:#131313;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Deliveries of Gas Transported by Others represents scheduled delivery nominations. The volumes shown do not impact the overall page 520 system gas balance because the differences between scheduled delivery nominations and actual physical deliveries are captured in the 806 imbalances and are included in the numbers shown on lines 10 and 25 of page 520.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-12" id="fn-12" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Deliveries of Contract Storage Gas represents scheduled injection nominations by others. The volumes shown do not impact the overall page 520 system gas balance because the difference between scheduled storage injections nominations and actual physical volumes delivered into storage are captured in the 806 imbalances shown on lines 10 and 25</span>
        <span style="color:#131313;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-13" id="fn-13" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:3pt">
        <span style="color:#131313;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Gas Delivered as Imbalances reflects the gas recorded in account 806 that relates to OBA, Receiving Party, Shipper and Park and Loan imbalances and is shown as Gas Delivered to Others.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-14" id="fn-14" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml" style="margin-top:3pt">
        <span style="color:#131313;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:120%">Other Gas Delivered to Storage relates to system balancing.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-15" id="fn-15" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#111111;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">The Other Deliveries reflects gas used for purposes other than operating compressor stations plus working gas, change in line pack and gas used in other non-mainline projects.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-16" id="fn-16" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">Any monthly excess or deficiency of gas is refunded or collected in-kind through Northwest&#8217;s semi-annual fuel filing process.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-17" id="fn-17" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">The numbers shown on this page include any fuel usage and in-kind reimbursements associated with transmission and storage rate schedules.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
    <link:footnote xlink:type="resource" xlink:label="fn-18" id="fn-18" xml:lang="en" xlink:role="http://www.xbrl.org/2003/role/footnote">
      <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">
        <span style="color:#000000;font-family:'Arial',sans-serif;font-size:10pt;font-weight:400;line-height:105%">The numbers shown on this page are derived by taking the total volume of throughput and allocating it among the three contract categories (i.e. contracts with discounted rates, contracts with negotiated rates, and contracts with recourse rates) based on the percentage of gas transported for each contract type.</span>
      </div>
    </link:footnote>
